{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/896","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/896/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/896/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/896/events","html_url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/896","id":5852506427,"node_id":"I_kwDORhCjFc8AAAABXNYpOw","number":896,"title":"Na2so3_X_5_H2o (sodium sulfite hydrate) has the anhydrous CHEBI:86477 as its exact identity","user":{"login":"realmarcin","id":4625870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MjU4NzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4625870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin","html_url":"https://github.com/realmarcin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/realmarcin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-10-14T17:32:22Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T02:24:00Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Found in the review of PR #881.\n\n**The problem:** `data/ingredients/mapped/Na2so3_X_5_H2o.yaml` (a sodium sulfite hydrate) has identifier and ontology mapping `CHEBI:86477`, sodium sulfite (anhydrous), at `SYNONYM_MATCH`, with an SSSOM `skos:exactMatch`.\n\n**Why it's wrong:** `MAPPING_SEMANTICS.md` §3 forbids mapping a hydrate to its anhydrous parent as an exact identity.\n\n**Consequence:** because `Na2so3` carries the same id, PR #881's move of the \"anhydrous sodium sulfite\" names from `Na2so3_X_5_H2o` to `Na2so3` changes nothing for CultureMech or the KG.\n\n**Existing tracking:** the only trace is the `HYDRATE_FAMILY_UNREVIEWED` row in `mappings/duplicate_identifier_baseline.tsv`. #321 is closed, and I found no open issue for this record.\n\n**Fix:** follow the §3 decision procedure.\n- If ChEBI has a term for this hydrate, ground to it.\n- Otherwise, preserve a distinct `cas:` or `kgmicrobe.compound:` identity with a CLOSE_MATCH parent of CHEBI:86477.\n\nThen update the SSSOM rows, the duplicate baseline and a mapping-change receipt.\n\n\n\n## Update 2026-10-14 (second review of #881)\n\n- **Correction to the suggested fix above:** where no ChEBI term exists, §3 step 2 needs three rows (see #897 for why `closeMatch` is wrong):\n  - the `cas:` or `kgmicrobe.compound:` identity;\n  - a `skos:broadMatch` (NARROW_MATCH) to CHEBI:86477;\n  - the Rule B1 registry row.\n- **More of the same defect:** `MIM:Na2so3`'s SSSOM `other` carries `Na2SO3 x 5 H2O`.\n  - It is not a YAML synonym of `Na2so3`, so it came in from kg-microbe labels.\n  - It is baselined under Rule K.\n  - It should leave when this record is split.\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/896/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/896/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}